\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Round 2}. Left: mod-9 target---the digit-sum (scaffold) donor solves it in 200 steps with no plateau, while the mod-3 (answer) donor is slower than scratch; mismatched/control donors show only mild generic acceleration. Middle: the dissociation mirrored on mod 11. Right: the magnitude curriculum---a converged short-operand stage makes the unlearnable 6-digit task trivial (f95 $=$ 600), while a pre-snap stage donates its coset and entrenches.}}{12}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
